<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 1.092 off UK's FTSE 100 index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 1.092 off UK's FTSE 100 index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE-100 stocks go ex-dividend on Monday and the effect was to take 1.092 points off in early trading. The calculations were based on net dividends.</p>
<p>						 DIVIDEND   INDEX</p>
<p>						 (PENCE)    EFFECT</p>
<p>		 COMPANY			  Net     Gross</p>
<p> * Carlton Communications	 4.90    0.169</p>
<p> * Railtrack Group		 14.80    0.421</p>
<p> * Thames Water		     23.20    0.502</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5113</p>
</text>
